From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 WebAuthn steps for the host: phone, security key, this Mac (ABI 1.68)

Engine side of docs/FEATURE-SPECS/PASSKEYS-AND-SITE-PERMISSIONS.md, part 1.
The owner's report: Microsoft sign-in says "Face, fingerprint, PIN or
security key: your device will open a security window", and nothing opens.

Why. A request's UI is AuthenticatorRequestDialogModel, whose SetStep opens
Chromium's dialog through AuthenticatorRequestDialogViewController::Create
(chrome/browser/ui/views/webauthn/
authenticator_request_dialog_view_controller_views.cc). Create returns null
without a WebContentsModalDialogManager on the tab, and a bridge tab has
none (browserless_tab_helpers.cc attaches no Browser UI helpers). The
request itself ran: the authenticators were discovered and the model went
through its steps, with nobody to show them or to answer, until the relying
party's timeout.

What. rearc::AttachWebAuthnPrompt, called from
ChromeAuthenticatorRequestDelegate's constructor, observes the model. Each
step with UI goes to the host as JSON (ReArcEngineSetWebAuthnCallback):
the ways to sign in, the QR code's text for a phone, a security key's PIN
entry with its errors and attempts, account choice, Bluetooth off or
denied, the errors. ReArcWebAuthnRespond calls the model as the dialog's
buttons do (chrome/browser/ui/webauthn/sheet_models.cc: each sheet's
OnAccept, OnCancel and OnBack), checked against the step that is shown.
The steps have names of the ABI's own, so a pin bump that renumbers
Chromium's enum does not change the host. A request that needs no dialog
(passkey autofill on a sign-in page) sends nothing. Without a host, or for
a page that is no registry tab, a request that reaches a step with UI is
cancelled instead of left waiting. Everything else stays Chromium's: the
transports (hybrid over Bluetooth with the tunnel service, USB HID, the
platform authenticators), the relying party checks, timeouts.

This Mac. The profile authenticator (keys in the Secure Enclave, Touch ID
or the login password) needs no Apple browser entitlement, only the
keychain access group <team>.<bundle id>.webauthn in the app's signature
(device/fido/mac/touch_id_context.mm). No ReArc build was signed with it,
so the authenticator was never offered; shell/scripts/icloud-signing.sh now
adds the group when the provisioning profile allows it. Chromium builds
the group's name from the branding's MAC_TEAM_ID. A release engine's
branding has it (build-engine-release.sh); the overlay's own, which the dev
engine uses, has none, and the group was ".com.rearc.browser.webauthn".
ChromeWebAuthenticationDelegate::TouchIdAuthenticatorConfigForProfile now
asks rearc::WebAuthnKeychainAccessGroup, which reads the team from the
running app's signature (com.apple.developer.team-identifier) when the
branding has none, so a signed dev build behaves as a release does. An
unsigned or ad hoc build is as before.

iCloud Keychain needs com.apple.developer.web-browser.public-key-credential
(device/fido/mac/icloud_keychain_sys.mm), which ReArc does not have, and
the page's NSWindow. ConfigureNSWindow found the window through a Views
widget, which a bridge tab is not in; it now falls back to
WebContents::GetTopLevelNativeWindow, so nothing else is missing the day
the entitlement is granted.

Google Password Manager steps (the enclave, its PIN and recovery windows)
are reported as "unsupported": they need a signed-in Chrome profile with
password sync, which a ReArc profile is not.

Built into the release engine on 2026-11-18 (overlay 85a7a97594,
out/ReArc-codecs-arm64): the framework exports both functions and
engine/tests/check_abi168_imports.py passes. Nothing here has run: the
flows need the host's sheet on screen, a real phone and a security key.

Touches: chrome/app/framework.exports, chrome/app/framework.order,
chrome/browser/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/{rearc_abi_internal.h,
rearc_engine_abi.h, rearc_engine_abi.mm, rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm,
rearc_services_abi.cc, rearc_webauthn.cc (new), rearc_webauthn.h (new)},
chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_authenticator_request_delegate.cc,
chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_web_authentication_delegate.cc.
Applies after tab/096 (the same lines of the export lists, BUILD.gn and the
ABI header).

Bridge 0.78.0, ABI 1.68, feature webauthn_prompts. No struct changes.

Last rebased: 2026-11-18 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.109 (overlay 67d25d5cf4).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

